# EI + ROBOT

This directory contains the paper implementation of direct expected
improvement (EI) with ranked ROBOT trust regions in normalized simulator-output
space.

At each BO batch the code fits the scalar detectability GP, optionally refits
the output GPs used by ROBOT, scores a shared candidate pool, processes the
ranked regions in order, and evaluates the selected simulations concurrently.
The included CSV files provide the initial O5a/O5b/O5c training data. NMMA SVD
models and the prior file are not stored in this repository.

## Environment

Install the Python requirements and NMMA, then set the external paths:

```bash
export NMMA_WORKDIR=/path/to/nmma/source/checkout
export SVD_PATH=/path/to/svdmodels
export PRIOR_FILE=/path/to/priors/Bu2019lm.prior
export OUTPUT_BASE="$PWD/out"
```

`NMMA_SVD_PATH`, `NMMA_PRIOR_FILE`, and `BO_OUTPUT_BASE` are accepted as
backward-compatible aliases.

## Paper configuration

```bash
python -u run_bo.py \
  --seed 1 \
  --n-iterations 80 \
  --output-folder out/direct_ei_all_regions_seed1 \
  --acquisition ROBOT_DIRECT_EI \
  --robot-distance-mode tail_l1 \
  --robot-tau-quantile 75 \
  --robot-initial-length 0.6 \
  --robot-success-tolerance 10 \
  --robot-failure-tolerance 32 \
  --robot-n-regions 5 \
  --robot-batch-regions 5 \
  --robot-candidates-per-region 1 \
  --parallel-simulations 5 \
  --candidate-samples 1500 \
  --direct-gp-restarts 5 \
  --refit-output-gps \
  --output-gp-refit-every 1 \
  --no-plots \
  --checkpoint-every 1 \
  --scoring-progress-every 0
```

This uses five ranked regions, selects at most one candidate per region, runs
up to five simulations concurrently, and refits the output GPs after every
completed batch. `--n-iterations` counts BO batches, not selected simulations;
each batch produces zero to five events depending on feasibility.

The base pool contains 1,500 uniform inputs because the uniform count equals
the total candidate count.

## Multiple seeds

```bash
python -u run_multi_seed.py \
  --seeds 1-3 \
  --n-iterations 80 \
  --output-root out/paper_ei_robot \
  --no-plots
```

Each run writes its event table, checkpoint, and NMMA products beneath its
output directory. Resume an interrupted run with identical settings and
`--resume`.
